  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes QFM‑CommNet, a quantum‑walk‑inspired Fourier operator framework for dynamic community detection. On datasets up to 100K nodes, it reports modularity 0.561 ± 0.010, NMI 0.739 ± 0.009, and ARI 0.671 ± 0.011, outperforming classical baselines such as Infomap and GNN+modularity loss. However, all experiments are classical; quantum elements (e.g., QAOA with p ≤ 3 on a 20‑qubit Qiskit simulator) are only mentioned conceptually and not empirically evaluated.",
