        "data_preprocessing_details": "Synthetic graphs are undirected and unweighted with isolated nodes removed and community size distribution normalized. Social networks are directed and unweighted with timestamp alignment and duplicate interaction removal. Biological networks use weighted undirected edges with edge weights normalized and low-confidence interactions pruned at threshold 0.05. Financial networks use rolling-window Pearson correlation, Fisher-z transformation, and sparsification at the 0.1 quantile.",
